title: "How Strong Is a Verified Tax Code? A Critical Study of Formalizing Philippine Tax Rules in Lean 4, with a Proven Certificate Checker"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hernandez
    given-names: Aaron Y.
    affiliation: BSANHS
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of computational parts of the Philippine National
  Internal Revenue Code, with sound and complete certificate checkers, measured
  studies of untrusted engines, five kernel-checked loophole findings, and a
  generated battery of 274 kernel-checked propositions.
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
  - rules as code
  - certifying algorithms
  - tax law
  - Philippines
  - large language models
